.SH RETURN VALUE
If
.I key-code
corresponds to a function key defined
by the application
or the terminal type in use,
.B \%keybound
allocates and returns a string
that must be freed by the application.
.B \%keybound
returns
.I NULL
if
.I key-code
is not positive,
if it does not correspond to a key code definition,
if
.I count
is negative or not less than the number of bindings of
.IR key-code ","
or if no screen has been initialized.
